    "created_at": "2019-11-28T02:56:03Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-11-28T03:23:12Z",
    "body": "Well, I&nbsp;looked&nbsp;through git&nbsp;history all&nbsp;the&nbsp;way&nbsp;back to&nbsp;2009, and&nbsp;“new&nbsp;`HTMLDocument`” wasn’t&nbsp;really ever&nbsp;used, it was always “new&nbsp;`Document`, whose&nbsp;<var>type</var>&nbsp;is&nbsp;`\"html\"`”, or “Create&nbsp;a&nbsp;new&nbsp;`Document`&nbsp;node, and&nbsp;mark&nbsp;it as&nbsp;being an&nbsp;**HTML&nbsp;document**”, both&nbsp;of&nbsp;which are&nbsp;equivalent.\r\n\r\nThis&nbsp;means&nbsp;that a&nbsp;`Document`&nbsp;instance’s&nbsp;inheritance is&nbsp;tied to&nbsp;its&nbsp;[`type`](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-type).\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI&nbsp;don’t really&nbsp;know how&nbsp;to&nbsp;specify&nbsp;that in&nbsp;a&nbsp;sane&nbsp;manner.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
